From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mstask: idle wait, priority, trigger strings, run times, IsOfType (3551)

mstask: SetIdleWait, SetPriority, GetTriggerString, GetRunTimes, IsOfType

ITask::SetIdleWait and SetPriority (IDLE/NORMAL/HIGH/REALTIME only) mark the task dirty so Save keeps them.
ITask::GetTriggerString and ITaskTrigger::GetTriggerString describe a trigger in English. ITask::GetRunTimes
lists the run times in a range by repeating the GetNextRunTime search from a given start (the search was
split out of GetNextRunTime). ITaskScheduler::IsOfType activates the work item and answers S_OK for IID_ITask,
S_FALSE for other types. Get/SetErrorRetryCount/Interval stay E_NOTIMPL: the conformance tests record that.
